})` are injective MPS of bond dimension `χ = 2` (bond Schmidt spectrum `(1/2, 1/2)`, transfer gap `1/3`), covariant for `G = U(1) ⋊ ℤ₂` with `ω_α(S^z) = +1/2 = s = −ω_β(S^z)`; the sharp domain wall in the `ℂ²` factor lies in `𝒦_{αβ}` and has `D_xφ = 0` at every site, so it satisfies (K-TAIL) with `C_K = 0` while its tail vacua are not product states (ace-ld-r3 F1). | **PROVED** | D2(a), D9(a), D13, D26 | theory/ace-ld.md ⟨1⟩4.⟨2⟩9(b) | theory/checks/ace_ld_check.py LD-C7(e) certifies the HYPOTHESIS (K-TAIL) on the D16 instance (\|\|D_xφ\|\| per-site ratios 0.20871 on both sides, C_K = 0.209, red-armed by --red-c7-orientation at C_K = 2525); the conclusion is exact algebra and needs no gate.  The refuting counterexample to the χ=1 form is verified numerically in ace-ld-r3.md F1(b). |

